<title>USA: Fed expected to stay out of open market again.</title>
<headline>Fed expected to stay out of open market again.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-08-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Federal Reserve was expected to refrain from intervening in the open market on Tuesday, as its add need appears to have been met, analysts said.</p>
<p>The Fed passed on intervention on Monday.</p>
<p>Fed watchers said Thursday's $4 billion, seven-day system repurchase agreements were enough to cover the add need for the first half of the two-week reserve period, which ends on Wednesday.</p>
<p>Federal funds were trading at the Fed's 5-1/2 percent target.</p>
<p>((--Steven Scheer, N.A. Treasury Desk, 212-859-1867))</p>
